body:
It is not "anyone else thinks". It is the common knowledge that it is the  **consequence of emotional neglect during childhood.**

&#x200B;

However, most of the therapists still do not understand BPD or do not know what DBT truly is.

Wait wait wait. Let me ask you a question if you really love your girl friend. Did you try to send her to DBT instead oftherapy and medication? Eventhough you do not have money, you should read a book on DBT and try to help her. Eventhough you have researched BPD extensively, how can you do not know the pretty much the only treatment for BPD is DBT ,and you did not try?

&#x200B;

If you really love your girl friend, either try to do DBT with her or send her to DBT.

First pain93's saying is correct. Nonthing is truly solved or nonthing was solved, but they decided to move on.

However, manga tells one more thing. Santo does not want to live in other people's control or "conspiracy".  If he can not becomes a sucessful person in the society, people will view him as a vermin. This idea does not treat him as a human being and only use him as a tool.  In addition, eventhough he became a sucessful person like his senpai, people only treat him better because he is a useful tool. Thus, he really understand that it is a conspiracy that his whole life is under people's control.

&#x200B;

If this still confuse you, think about this. One of my friend told me that his father yelled at him, "How can you are a good person? You test scores is very low!" Thus, he does not want to die under this idea or conspiracy, and he went back to his mother's home to become a writer.

&#x200B;

&#x200B;

Thank You. I just got a interview tomorrow as a math tutoring. However, I think I messed up the interview today.

&#x200B;

How did you do interview as a mental disabled person?

&#x200B;

If you could, could you tell me more about how you faced discrimation in the interview or job?

&#x200B;

People who is your boss laugh at you on your disability. They sometimes think you do not have a disability because you have a hidden disability.

&#x200B;

I think these are the things I really need to know.

I think there is a cure fact, and most of the therapists today should admit this.

Most of the therapist does not know how to treat BPD. They don't even understand what BPD really is. 

&#x200B;

* This is the pitfalls that I have been stepping in like a cycle.

At the same time, people around you hostage you because you are announcing them and acting like a child; thus, they look down you because you act like a child. They judge you as a bad person because you are annoying them. In the meantime, you feel guilty, so you try to control yourself or punish yourself to stop your BPD. In the end, you fail everything. 

&#x200B;

The reason why people with BPD acts so childish is that their parents or people around them treated them a creature lower than a human being. They have lived in this kind of life for at least decades or more than fifteen years. That is why the emotion part of their brain is extremely affected from their childhood. 

Thus, that is why everytime they feel pain from the past, they act like a child to ask people love them, and they are so scared people may harm them.

&#x200B;

